# Design System Standards

Follow `AGENTS.md` → **Design System Standards**. Tokens: `app/globals.css`.

## Quick reference

| Concern | Default |
|---------|---------|
| Font | Geist + Geist Mono (**do not change** when aligning sizes) |
| Size + radius scale | SonoJS tokens (**46px** default; 12px radius; not brand colors) |
| Control + surface radius | **12px** (`--radius: 0.75rem` / `rounded-md` / `rounded-lg`) · tooltip ~6px |
| Button heights | xs 32 · sm 40 · **default 46** · lg 52 · icon `size-[46px]` |
| Input / Select | `h-[46px]` · `px-3` · `rounded-md` · `border-border/70` |
| Cards | `border-border/70` · `rounded-[12px]` · `shadow-soft` |
| Checkbox / Switch | `size-4` · switch `h-[1.15rem]` × `w-8` |
| Body / button text | 16 / 14 medium (typography tokens frozen) |
| Icon default | Lucide 16px |
| Content max / sidebar | 1280px / 240px |
| Spacing | 4px scale |
| Responsive | Same 46px controls on mobile/tablet/desktop; adapt width/stack only |

Prefer changing a shared token over editing every call site. Preserve installable component APIs and intentional variants. When aligning sizes: update heights, padding, and radius only — never fonts or `--primary` colors.

## Primary Button Contrast

- Text on primary must contrast with **button background**, not page theme.
- Default blue (`#2563EB` light / `#396EF0` dark): `--primary-foreground: #FFFFFF` in light **and** dark.
- Never force black label on blue primary just because the site is in dark mode.
- Hover / active / disabled stay readable; use `--primary` + `--primary-foreground`.
- Light custom primaries may need a dark foreground; default brand blue does not.
- WCAG AA: 4.5:1 normal / 3:1 large.

## Code blocks

- Use `ComponentSource` + `--code-*` chrome tokens; syntax via shiki `dark-plus` (VS Code Dark+).
- Geist Mono, 14px / 1.65 / weight 400 / tab-size 2 (VS Code default size); no wrap — scroll horizontally.
- Syntax colors independent of brand `--primary`. Dark block OK in light and dark site themes.
- Highlighter: `lib/highlight-code.ts` → theme `dark-plus`.
